Z||000000||danny boy||01-15-2001||08:18 PM||||  In april '99 I bought a Dodge Stealth twin turbo. Since then I have been comepletely ignoring my Fieros and even sold my 86 coupe<BR>(one of the most painful things I have ever done).  When I drove my Fiero and pulled up along another Fiero I'd atleast get a wave and a smile. If I happened to be in a parking lot and another owner pulled up<BR> The conversatoin was a friendly one. "How long have you had it,how many others do you have(most people have more than one),whats done to it?" Not 3Kgt people. Im not saying theyre all bad,but they are definately not like Fiero people.<BR>  ||||reg||7
Z||000001||Cheever2||01-15-2001||08:24 PM||||I hear ya.  At the car wash, someone always comes up to talk about one they had.  One guy with a 4x4 said he got too many tickets in his Fiero, so he decided to play offroad instead.  I'm not so sure that's any less expensive, based on my experience.<BR><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I>||||reg||6
Z||000002||FieroMaster88||01-16-2001||02:35 AM||||There must not be too many Fiero people around here.  I wave at other Fiero owners on the road and they look at me like I am crazy!!!  Every once in a while someone will ask about the car.  But for the most part, people just have smart comments.  I have a friend with a Honda Civic who picks on it, but he still cant beat it!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">  <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster86<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles<BR>84 Indy Fiero (restoration Project)||||reg||1
